    "explanation": "To both parties. This was a solo metered RydeX trip (TRP-00718), and the route is decided by the GPS trace, which is unimpaired: 247 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 s, so none of the POL-RD-07 limbs is met and the POL-RD-10(3) escalation route is not engaged. Between the first fix at 15:18:40 and the last at 15:59:40 the trace records 26.84 km against the platform's booked optimal of 20.7 km, an excess of 6.14 km or 29.66%. That clears both POL-RD-01 gates (over 20% and over 0.8 km), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED on this trip's own evidence. It does not reach the materiality gates (over 50% or over 8.0 km), so the POL-RD-06 pattern test is not engaged; consulted anyway, the driver profile shows deviation_flags_90d of 0 across 250 completed trips in 90 days, so no repeat pattern, no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral arise. The driver's chat message of 15:32:50 and his own statement both confirm he took the longer route to collect another passenger. No rider instruction appears anywhere in the bundle, so POL-RD-04 gives nothing, and POL-RD-12 does not apply because trip_record.vehicle_type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL (solo_optimal_distance_km is null), so the distance driven to collect the second passenger is not excluded from the excess. No traffic advisory covers this trip — EV-ADVIS-00718-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — but the driver cites no advisory and asserts no traffic cause at all, so under POL-RD-13(2) this is a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, POL-RD-10(5) does not fire, and the deviation stands at the measured figure. The fare model is METERED, so POL-RD-02 runs: recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 20.7 + 0.28 x 31) x 1.0 (the surge multiplier read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP/tolls + 0 waiting fee - 0 promo = 28.805. Charged_total is 36.18, so the refund is 36.18 - 28.805 = 7.375, rounded up to SGD 7.40. That is above the 0.50 de minimis floor and 20.4% of the amount charged, well below the 90% share that would license a FULL_REFUND, so the outcome is a partial refund of SGD 7.40. Nothing is added on top: the fare breakdown carries no ERP gantries (off-route and on-route totals both 0.00) and no airport surcharge on a trip that ends at, rather than originates at, an airport, so POL-RD-09 contributes nothing and no billing-integrity referral fires. On the alleged SGD 40 cash demand: no such line exists in the fare breakdown, no artifact supports it, and the rider expressly does not seek it, so it plays no part in either direction. The driver's admission of the detour is an admission against interest, but it corroborates only what the unimpaired trace already shows, so the deciding facts rest on the trip record, the trace and the fare breakdown, all at weight 1.0, and confidence is capped at 1.0. Confidence 0.9. No referral is required by any clause."
