    "explanation": "Both advocates agree on the arithmetic, and so do I, so this is a ruling on the merits rather than on disputed evidence.\n\nThe deviation is established. The GPS trace EV-GPS-00718 records trace_distance_km 26.84 against the booked optimal of 20.7 km on the trip record EV-TRIP-00718, an excess of 6.14 km, 29.66% of optimal. POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km the governing field and forbids citing the rounded trip_record.actual_distance_km; on that measurement both gates are cleared (above 20% of optimal and above 0.8 km absolute), so a route deviation is ESTABLISHED. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07: 247 fixes at a 10-second sample interval, coverage 100%, an empty gaps array and max_gap_sec 0.0, so none of limbs (a) to (c) is met and the POL-RD-10(3) escalation route is not engaged. The excess is below both materiality gates (50% of optimal and 8.0 km absolute), so this is not a MATERIAL deviation and POL-RD-06 is not engaged; consulted anyway, the driver profile shows deviation_flags_90d 0 over completed_trips_90d 250, so no repeat pattern is established and no conduct referral arises on either advocate's reading.\n\nThe driver has no exculpation. POL-RD-04 does not run: the only chat message (EV-CHAT-00718) is the driver's own, sent at 15:32:50 with waypoint_hint null, and there is no rider instruction anywhere in the bundle, so limb (a) fails at the outset. POL-RD-12 does not run: vehicle_type is RYDE_X and solo_optimal_distance_km is null, so this is not a platform-matched pooled itinerary and the matched-itinerary baseline does not displace the 20.7 km booked optimal. POL-RD-03 cannot be run: the bundle's only traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-00718-01, is MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, with no payload and no corridor coverage. The driver asserts no external traffic cause at all - he attributes the route to the second passenger and says he has no advisory or rider instruction excusing it - so under POL-RD-13(2) the deviation stands at the measured figure, POL-RD-10(5) does not fire, and the absent advisory does not escalate the case. The driver's assertions of the extra passenger pickup do not fit any exculpatory clause, and the second passenger's collection is not a deviation the rider caused.\n\nRemedy under POL-RD-02. The fare is METERED and the surge multiplier, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier and nowhere else, is 1.0. recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 20.7 + 0.28 x 31) x 1.0, plus the 0.80 platform fee, plus 0 ERP/tolls, plus 0 waiting fee, less 0 promo = 28.805. Charged_total is 36.18 (EV-FARE-00718), so the refund is 36.18 - 28.805 = 7.375, rounded UP to SGD 7.40. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and 20.4% of the amount charged, far short of the 90% share that would license a FULL_REFUND. POL-RD-09 adds nothing on top: the fare breakdown carries no ERP gantries and no tolls (erp_lines total 0.00), and its airport_surcharge line is 0.0 on a trip that ends at rather than originates at an airport, so no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity correction arises; in any event off-route ERP is already comprehended in the charged_total less recomputed fare, and must never be stacked on it.\n\nOn the alleged SGD 40 cash demand: it appears on no line of the fare breakdown and in no message of the chat log, so it is unsupported and carries no weight; the rider does not seek it and it affects neither the arithmetic nor the outcome.\n\nConfidence: the deciding facts rest on the trip record, the GPS trace, the fare breakdown and the chat log, all COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0. The only impaired artifact is the MISSING advisory at weight 0.0, on which no finding rests, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and my confidence is 0.9, above the 0.70 escalation floor. No clause produces a referral on these facts, so the referrals list is empty."
